+## R17 control.72 — named expressions and head target metadata
+
+`robot.skills` publishes the thirteen existing `emotion_cycle::CYCLE` expressions separately from learned body skills, with Chinese meanings, native durations, and the head target ranges read from `kinematics::Model::alpha`. Those ranges are model references, not measured mechanical end stops. The console intersects them with its saved head amplitude and keeps all native calibration and actuator protection.
+
+`robot.do emotion_silent_<name>` selects that exact timeline in the same control-loop player without advancing R3's cycle and without opening another audio player. One atomic slot holds selection, generation and pending/playing/completed/cancelled phase; busy requests are refused, never queued. `emotion_status` reads it, and `emotion_cancel_<request_id>` cancels only that generation. A finite named expression does not need repeated client zero-twist writes; it still requires zero motion, fresh sensors and IMU, upright ready driving, Walk mode and an idle controller. Manual HOME, disabling, policy/mode changes, body skills, nonzero motion and sensor loss cancel playback through the existing loop. Nothing enables torque or performs HOME for AI. No new process, bus read, bus writer, or 50 Hz client loop is added. The matching native robotd update is required for the new names; API version 41 describes the extension, and version skew remains informational.
+
